// A list that yields, built only to be walked to its end by `sum`, `max` or
// `min`, is warned of (E0480), with the fix that walks the generator, which
// allocates nothing. A walk that may stop early, as `any` does, is left
// alone: the list's loop runs to its end first, and what it does would not
// all be done; so is a list of more than the loop.

fn main() = {
    val numbers = [1, 2, 3]
    val total = [for n in numbers { yield n * n }].sum()
    val most = [for n in numbers { if n < 3 then yield n }].max()
    val least = [for n in numbers { yield n }].min()
    val found = [for n in numbers { yield n }].any((n) => n > 1)
    val more = [0, for n in numbers { yield n }].sum()
    assert(total == 14 && most == 2 && least == 1 && found && more == 6)
}
